To move a character forward in Unity when the W key is pressed, you can use the following code snippet. This example assumes you have a basic understanding of Unity and C# scripting. Make sure to attach this script to your character GameObject.

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class MoveCharacter : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float speed = 5.0f;

    void Update()
    {
        if (Input.GetKey(KeyCode.W))
        {
            transform.Translate(Vector3.forward * speed * Time.deltaTime);
        }
    }
}
```

This script continuously checks if the W key is being pressed. If it is, the character moves forward at the specified speed. The `Time.deltaTime` ensures that the movement is frame rate independent, providing a smooth experience.
